      "body": "### Summary\n\nAdds a measured recipe for the AMD Radeon 8060S (Strix Halo, gfx1151) to the Qwen-Image 2.1 cookbook: one row in the hardware table and a `### Strix Halo (Radeon 8060S)` subsection next to the existing DGX Spark one.\n\nThe subsection records two platform prerequisites that are not obvious from the existing AMD guidance:\n\n- `TORCH_ROCM_AOTRITON_ENABLE_EXPERIMENTAL=1` — a **PyTorch** SDPA switch, not an SGLang flag. Without it PyTorch falls back from the Flash-efficient attention kernel and 1024x1024/40-step latency goes from ~155 s to more than 9 minutes on this GPU (measured).\n- `--attention-backend torch_sdpa` — the runtime resolves the backend to AITER by default, which is not verified on gfx1151.\n\n### Measurement\n\nSame methodology as the existing table: original checkpoint, 1024x1024, 40 steps, CFG 1, one RGBA PNG per request, median HTTP latency of three warm requests after a discarded warmup, excluding startup. Peak memory is the request-phase sample reported by the server.\n\n| Config | Median | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `torch_sdpa` + AOTriton env (row value) | 154.98 s | 3 runs: 154.93 / 154.98 / 155.11 |\n| `SGLANG_CACHE_DIT_ENABLED=true` (default MC=3) | 56.96 s | documented as an optional speed/fidelity trade |\n\nPlatform: Ubuntu 24.04.2, kernel 7.0.0-38-generic, PyTorch 2.9.1+rocm7.2.4 (HIP 7.2.53211), Radeon 8060S with 128 GB unified memory (the kernel reports a 512 MiB VRAM carve-out, GTT cap ~108 GiB). FP8 is unavailable on this GPU.\n\n### Scope and limits\n\n- Only numbers reproducible on **upstream main with merged features** are used. Custom Triton kernels from open PRs (#44037 / #46065 / #46515) are intentionally excluded, so the row is slower than our best local result.\n- **Edit** is left as `—`: `POST /v1/images/edits` returns 500 with `prompt_embeds ... NaN` on this base checkpoint, and `Qwen-Image-Edit-2511` weights are not available on the test machine. Transparent output is likewise unverified.\n- Cache-DiT quality: PSNR 28.4 dB at default settings vs 27.5 dB with `SGLANG_CACHE_DIT_MC=6`, measured with the CLI on the same prompt and seed.\n\n### Checklist\n\n- [x] Only `docs/` changed; no code or CI changes\n- [x] Follows `docs/AGENTS.md` (platform/OS/version stated, no guessed defaults, copy-pasteable commands)\n- [x] Latency stated with the same definition as the existing table\n- [x] Unverified items marked explicitly (`—`, \"remain unverified\")\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #40471111335](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40471111335)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40471111299](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40471111299)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:heavy_minus_sign: **No AMD PR run found for this commit**.<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
