      "additions": 30,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/395622a4ff1a6aac2af23e5ff78dfc3435a418e4/docs%2Fcookbook%2Fdiffusion%2FQwen-Image%2FQwen-Image-2.1.mdx",
      "changes": 30,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/contents/docs%2Fcookbook%2Fdiffusion%2FQwen-Image%2FQwen-Image-2.1.mdx?ref=395622a4ff1a6aac2af23e5ff78dfc3435a418e4",
      "deletions": 0,
      "filename": "docs/cookbook/diffusion/Qwen-Image/Qwen-Image-2.1.mdx",
      "patch": "@@ -63,6 +63,7 @@ batch size one. Explicit placement and attention overrides preserve each recipe.\n | RTX PRO 6000 96GB | Resident / Torch SDPA | 8.03 s | 9.63 s | 38.4 GiB |\n | RTX 4090 24GB | DiT and VAE resident, encoder layerwise offload / FlashAttention | 18.68 s | 21.68 s | 22.7 GiB |\n | DGX Spark 128GB unified | Resident / Torch SDPA | 35.36 s | 42.23 s | — (unified) |\n+| Radeon 8060S 128GB unified | Resident / Torch SDPA | 155.0 s | — | 16.8 GB (unified) |\n \n Measured with the original checkpoint on 2026-09-20 at 1024×1024, 40 steps, CFG 1, and one RGBA PNG per\n request. Times are median HTTP latency after warmup, including PNG serialization\n@@ -96,6 +97,35 @@ Generation, editing, transparent generation, and transparent editing were\n verified with PyTorch 2.13.0+cu130. Spark reports no separate VRAM usage in `nvidia-smi`.\n This recipe covers one Spark; multi-node deployment and batching remain unverified.\n \n+### Strix Halo (Radeon 8060S)\n+\n+Select **AMD Strix Halo** for one Radeon 8060S iGPU on Linux with ROCm 7.2. Use the\n+source installation above. The recommended configuration keeps the DiT and VAE\n+resident and uses Torch SDPA:\n+\n+```bash Command\n+TORCH_ROCM_AOTRITON_ENABLE_EXPERIMENTAL=1 sglang serve \\\n+  --model-path Qwen/Qwen-Image-2.1 \\\n+  --attention-backend torch_sdpa\n+```\n+\n+`TORCH_ROCM_AOTRITON_ENABLE_EXPERIMENTAL=1` is a PyTorch requirement on AMD iGPUs,\n+not an SGLang flag. Without it, PyTorch falls back from the Flash-efficient\n+attention kernel and 1024×1024/40-step latency rises from about 155 s to more\n+than 9 minutes in our tests. Pass `--attention-backend torch_sdpa` as well: the\n+default AITER path is not verified on this GPU.\n+\n+The GPU shares the 128 GB unified memory with the CPU. The kernel reports a\n+512 MiB VRAM carve-out (`mem_info_vram_total`) instead of separate VRAM use, so\n+CPU offload is unnecessary for the verified single-image workload. FP8\n+quantization is unavailable on this GPU.\n+\n+Generation was verified with PyTorch 2.9.1+rocm7.2.4 on Ubuntu 24.04 (kernel\n+7.0.0); editing and transparent output remain unverified. To trade a small\n+amount of fidelity for speed, enable Cache-DiT with `SGLANG_CACHE_DIT_ENABLED=true`:\n+the same request drops to about 57 s at the default cache settings, and quality\n+falls from 28.4 dB to 27.5 dB PSNR when `SGLANG_CACHE_DIT_MC` is raised to 6.\n+\n ### Batching\n \n Keep **Request batching → Off** and **Outputs → 1** for interactive use.",
